  ======================================================================
    s57 TUNING MISSION — MAKE IT A PROPER DIVERSIFIER
    Started: 2026-03-13
  ======================================================================

  === PROBLEM STATEMENT ===

  s57 (signal_timed_turbo_carry) is in 15 of 21 paper trading pools but is
  essentially break-even in live trading (-$464 realized, -$330 unrealized).

  In backtesting it looks amazing (+290% solo, 8.56 Sharpe) but this is
  misleading because:

  1. IT BLOCKS s56 VIA CROSS-STRATEGY TOKEN DEDUP — In the s56+s57 combined
     backtest, s57 takes 100% of trades. s56 gets ZERO. Root cause is NOT
     capital allocation — it's simulator.py line 570:
       `if state.position_manager.total_margin_for_token(token) > 0: continue`
     This prevents ANY strategy from entering a token another strategy holds.
     s57 (regime-agnostic) enters tokens first, blocking s56 on all 95 shared
     tokens. s56 can only access 6 perp-only tokens (ARC, FARTCOIN, etc).

  2. s56 IS REGIME-BLOCKED IN DOWNTRENDS (by design, not a bug) — s56 has
     REGIME_SIZE[DOWNTREND]=0.0 and REGIME_SIZE[CRISIS]=0.0. Per-token regime
     (not just BTC) determines tradability. In Feb 2026: 100% of BTC bars are
     DOWNTREND, but 66% of perp tokens have SOME non-DT bars. In March 2026:
     77% of tokens have non-DT bars. s56 solo still trades 54 times in Feb
     and 45 in March on the non-DT windows. But in the combo, s57 holds those
     tokens during the DT periods and the token dedup prevents s56 from entering
     when the regime opens briefly.

  3. s57's INTENDED ROLE IS TO FILL THE GAP — When s56 can't trade (downtrends),
     s57 should provide returns. This is actually ideal diversifier behavior:
     - s56 blocked ~30-100% of bars during DT months → s57 picks up the slack
     - Near-zero correlation (0.13) confirms different edge families
     - On ALL 20 of s56's worst days, s57 provided positive cushion (+1.6% avg)
     But currently the token dedup prevents them from coexisting.

  4. THE EDGE IS BASIS CONVERGENCE, NOT CARRY — Despite the name, funding
     income is only 0.5% of PnL. The real mechanism is:
     - Enter when perp-spot basis is elevated (z-score > 1.5)
     - Long spot + short perp
     - Profit when basis narrows (both legs win: 26% of trades)
     - Asymmetric trailing stops create directional tilt (spot 3.5 ATR, perp 3.0 ATR)
     - 79% win rate, 4.6x payoff in backtest

  5. PAPER TRADING IS FLAT — 33 open pairs with near-zero P&L. The basis
     conditions that the backtest exploited may not be present in current
     market. Or position sizes are too small for the edge.

  === KEY FINDINGS FROM ANALYSIS ===

