  - On s56's 20 worst days, s57 cushioned 20/20 times (avg +1.6%)
  - Cuts MaxDD from -3.3% to -0.5% when combined

  === TUNING DIMENSIONS ===

  D0. CROSS-STRATEGY TOKEN DEDUP (root cause — highest priority)
  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Problem: simulator.py line 570 prevents two strategies from holding the same
  token. s57 holds 8-15 tokens at any time, blocking s56 from entering those.
  Over 12 months, s57 rotates through 42 unique tokens — most of the liquid
  universe. s56 solo trades 71 tokens, 65 overlap with s57's combined universe.

  Options:
  a) REMOVE token dedup entirely — allow s56 perp short + s57 spot long/perp short
     on same token. Risk: correlated positions, but they're different edge families.
  b) EXEMPT combined strategies from dedup — s57 (combined) doesn't block s56 (perp).
     Rationale: s57 is delta-neutral, it doesn't directionally compete with s56.
  c) REDUCE s57 max_positions to 5-8 — fewer tokens blocked at any time.
     Trade-off: less s57 diversification benefit.
  d) Give s56 PRIORITY over s57 — process s56 entries first, s57 fills remaining.

  D1. CAPITAL ALLOCATION (secondary)
  ───────────────────────────────────────────
  Once dedup is fixed, ensure both strategies get fair capital share.
  Current: s57 uses 2 position slots per pair (spot+perp = 30 slots for 15 pairs).

  Options:
  a) Reduce s57 max_positions from 15 to 5-8 (limit its capital use)
  b) Count combined pairs as 1 position slot instead of 2
  c) Set s57 weight < 1.0 (e.g., 0.3-0.5) to allocate less capital
  d) Introduce a per-strategy capital cap (e.g., s57 can use max 30% of equity)

  D2. POSITION SIZING
  ───────────────────────────────────────────
  Problem: In paper trading, s57 enters with small sizes that don't generate
  meaningful P&L. In backtest, $10K+ per leg.

  Options:
  a) Increase size_multiplier floor (currently 0.3, maybe 1.0 minimum)
  b) Increase capital_split (currently 0.5 — maybe asymmetric: 0.6 spot, 0.4 perp)
  c) Adjust cap_multiplier to allow larger positions on high-conviction entries

  D3. ENTRY TIMING
  ───────────────────────────────────────────
  Problem: In current market, basis conditions may not be as extreme as
  historical backtest. Entry signal may need re-tuning.

  Options:
  a) Lower basis z-score threshold (currently 1.5, maybe 1.0)
  b) Add alternative entry conditions (vol spike, cross-TF divergence alone)
  c) Widen the entry window (more tokens eligible)
  d) Check if entry signal fires at all in March 2026 paper trading

  D4. TRAILING STOP ASYMMETRY
  ───────────────────────────────────────────
  The spot trail (3.5 ATR) vs perp trail (3.0 ATR) creates directional alpha.
  This could be tuned to be more or less delta-neutral depending on goal.

  Options:
  a) Make both trails equal (pure delta-neutral — less directional, lower return)
  b) Widen the asymmetry (more directional — higher return but more correlated)
  c) Add profit-based trail progression (currently static)

  D5. HOLD PERIOD
  ───────────────────────────────────────────
  All trades hold exactly 48h (no_stop_bars=48). The stop activates and fires
  immediately when protection expires.

  Options:
  a) Shorten no_stop_bars to 24h (faster turnover, more trades)
  b) Lengthen to 72-96h (let basis converge more fully)
  c) Dynamic no_stop_bars based on basis z-score at entry

  === IMPLEMENTATION PLAN ===

  Phase 1: Backtest ALL Options (< 2 hours) — SWEEP FIRST, DECIDE AFTER

  Run the s56+s57 12-month combo backtest under each option below.
  Record: total return, Sharpe, Calmar, MaxDD, per-strategy trades + PnL,
  correlation between s56 and s57 daily returns.

  OPTIONS TO BACKTEST:

  A. TOKEN DEDUP CHANGES (simulator.py line 570)

    A1. REMOVE dedup entirely
        - Allow both strategies to hold same token simultaneously
        - s56 perp short + s57 spot long + s57 perp short on same token = OK
        - Risk: triple exposure on same token, concentration

    A2. EXEMPT combined strategies from dedup
        - If existing position is from a combined (delta-neutral) strategy,
          don't block other strategies from entering
        - Rationale: s57 is delta-neutral, not directionally competing
        - Only s57-type strategies get the exemption

    A3. EXEMPT based on market type mismatch
        - Allow same token if strategies use different markets
        - s56 (perp-only) + s57 (combined spot+perp) = allowed
        - s56 (perp) + s60 (perp) = still blocked (same market)
        - Most flexible, least risky

    A4. KEEP dedup, reduce s57 max_positions
        - Sweep: max_positions = 3, 5, 8 (currently 15)
        - Fewer tokens blocked → s56 can enter more
        - Trade-off: less s57 diversification

    A5. REGIME-DYNAMIC DEDUP
        - Dedup strictness changes based on per-token regime
        - In DOWNTREND/CRISIS: RELAX dedup (s57 doesn't block s56)
          because s56 needs every tradeable window it can get
        - In UPTREND/QUIET: KEEP dedup (avoid over-concentration)
          because s56 has plenty of opportunities
        - In RANGE: configurable (test both)
        - Implementation: check regime of the token at current bar,
          skip dedup if regime is in a "relaxed" set

    A6. STRATEGY-PRIORITY DEDUP
        - Assign priority per strategy per regime
        - In UPTREND: s56 priority > s57 (s56 thrives, give it tokens)
        - In DOWNTREND: s57 priority > s56 (s56 is blocked anyway)
        - Higher priority strategy's positions don't block lower priority
        - Lower priority strategy's positions DO block higher priority
        - Effectively: the right strategy "owns" tokens in its best regime

    A7. DYNAMIC MAX_POSITIONS BY REGIME
        - s57 max_positions varies by BTC regime:
          UPTREND: 3-5 (minimal, let s56 dominate)
          RANGE: 8 (balanced)
          DOWNTREND: 15 (fill the gap, s56 can't trade anyway)
          CRISIS: 15 (same)
          QUIET: 5-8 (balanced)
        - No simulator change needed — can be implemented in s57 strategy
          by zeroing entry_mask when open positions exceed regime limit

  B. CAPITAL ALLOCATION VARIANTS (on top of best A option)

    B1. Equal weight (s56=1.0, s57=1.0) — current default
    B2. s56-heavy (s56=1.0, s57=0.5)
    B3. s57-heavy (s56=0.5, s57=1.0)
    B4. Dynamic: s57 weight = 1.5 in DOWNTREND, 0.5 in UPTREND

  C. s57 MAX_POSITIONS SWEEP (on top of best A option)

    C1. max_positions = 3 (minimal footprint)
    C2. max_positions = 5
    C3. max_positions = 8
    C4. max_positions = 10
    C5. max_positions = 15 (current)

